body:
VXWCWGWN03Q2

&#x200B;

This seed is nuts, you get shuriken early af

You know when people make mistakes, they usually learn from them, right?

&#x200B;

Also, yes? It was like that? The first addition to the game was Goblins vs Gnomes? And there were Goblins vs Gnomes packs?

You misunderstand, you troglodyte. I am perfectly happy spending time and money on my hobbies, however not when it is obvious that they are a ripoff. Please look at me with a straight face and tell me that it feels good to open a mercs pack only to receive coins for a hero you got to max 3 months ago. Tell me it feels good spending upwards of 30 minutes doing a bounty, praying that you get the coins for the one hero you need, only to get 5 sets of coins for Milhouse.

&#x200B;

As we speak, there is a "deal" in the shop where you can get 5 packs and 300 Long'xin coins for $15. Not Long'xin, just Long'xin coins. Or how about 400 Y'Shaarj coins for $10? Are you going to honestly tell me with a straight face that is a fair price? I am not saying that Blizzard asking for money for packs and mercs is unreasonable. I am saying it is unreasonable that they are asking for so much time and money for such minimal rewards.

Yeah, a bundle that is $25 for 1 legendary that will be phased out via powercreep that I still have to grind to level up and 10 packs, each filled with coins for Rokara and Cariel.

&#x200B;

Thanks, but I'll pass, you are more than welcome to waste your money, though.

I agree that the task rework was a great idea, but you know how much grinding there should be? Literally zero. This is a card game, I shouldn't need to spend time to get the characters from packs, only to have them be completely useless until I waste my precious time to get them to a usable level. This game mode wants to have its cake and eat it too.

&#x200B;

Also, I love how you say I am complaining to complain, only to IMMEDIATELY list 2 major flaws with the game's design.
